      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ttf2xe'
    '|a||Because it''s a checklist. It tells you exactly where to look when a market goes wrong: market power, a missing price, hidden information.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15049id'
    '|b||What it can''t tell you is that any real market is efficient. Or that the result is fair.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1bmb2te'
    '|a||And two famous readings pull in opposite directions. Greenwald and Stiglitz showed in 1986 that with imperfect information, markets are almost never efficient, even by a planner''s realistic standards.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:za7pry'
    '|b||Hayek''s old point cuts the other way: the model behind the theorem assumes everyone knows everything, but the real case for prices is that they gather what nobody knows.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:17lb6ej'
    '|b||And a broken assumption isn''t a free pass for the state, which faces the same missing information.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1h5pshm'
    '|a||How sure are we? The theorem itself is a proof: consensus. How close real markets come to it is contested, case by case.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:yynjny'
    '|a||Want to see why the theorem is true? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1vc7o73'
    '|a||Suppose some other allocation makes someone better off and no one worse off.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Whoever is better off couldn''t afford it at the market prices, or they''d have chosen it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1lw8rea'
    '|a||Everyone else would pay at least as much for it as they pay now.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:racxo9'
    '|a||So it costs more than everyone''s income combined. More than the economy has: impossible.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:p2nirm'
    '|a||New case: ride-hailing, where every car adds jams nobody pays for. Efficient?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1xfhpe0'
    '|a||No: a cost has no price. The jams are a cost the fare leaves out, so too many rides are taken.':
